---
source: crates/cli/tests/native.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
A number in binary, octal, decimal, hex or any base from 2 to 36

Usage: tw base [OPTIONS] [VALUE]

Arguments:
  [VALUE]  The input itself; stdin when left out, or -

Options:
      --from <N>      The input's base, 2 to 36; 0 reads it from a 0x, 0o or 0b prefix, else decimal
      --to <N>        Write the number in this base only, 2 to 36; 0 for the usual bases
  -g, --group <N>     Put a space between groups of this many digits, from the right; 0 for none
  -u, --upper         Write digits above 9 in uppercase
      --bits <BITS>   Also read the number as a signed and unsigned integer of this many bits
                      [possible values: 8, 16, 32, 64, 128]
  -i, --input <FILE>  Read the input from FILE
      --json          Write the result as JSON
      --no-newline    Do not end text output with a newline
  -h, --help          Print help
